        "desc": "Originating in the hill ranges of South Tripura and flowing southwest to empty into Sandwip Channel in the Bay of Bengal, the Feni River serves as a vital international watercourse. The meandering river valley is bordered by fertile sandbars, emerald paddy fields, coconut palm groves, and traditional fishing hamlets where fishermen cast traditional throw-nets from graceful wooden sampans. In the upper reaches near border crossings, low rolling green ridges flank the clear turquoise waters, providing postcard-perfect pastoral vistas. Taking an afternoon country boat trip along the gentle current allows travelers to witness river dolphins, waterbirds, and tranquil rural lifestyles far from urban noise. The serene corridor captures the idyllic essence of Bangladesh's timeless riverine geography.",
